[size=6][b]Squad Tactics — command your squad in SpaceBourne 2[/b][/size]

In SpaceBourne 2 your ground squad trails behind you in a loose crowd. With Squad Tactics you give them orders the way Ready or Not does: pick everyone, a team or one soldier, aim at a spot and tell them what to do there (move, hold and cover, stack up on a door and clear the room). And while you walk, one or two of them lead the way: ahead of you down a corridor, against the wall, crouched and watching, leapfrogging on as you catch up. When shooting starts, they fight the game's own way.

[b]Links:[/b] [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics]GitHub[/url] · [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/18]Nexus[/url] · UE4SS Lua mod · works alone or with the rest of the realism set.
[b]Install the whole realism set in one go:[/b] the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]).

[line]
[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Squad orders[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Aim and tap Z.[/b] The order that fits what you aim at, given at once: the floor or a wall means [i]move here[/i], a door means [i]stack up[/i], one of your soldiers means [i]cover him[/i], the sky means [i]fall in[/i].
[*][b]Hold Z for the list.[/b] The orders appear next to the crosshair. Move the mouse up and down to pick one, left and right to pick who gets it, and let go of Z to give it. The view stays still while you choose.
[*][b]Who: 0.[/b] All (gold), the red team, the blue team, or the one or two soldiers nearest the spot. The teams are split by your crew order (red = the first two).
[*][b]The orders:[/b]
    - [i]Move here[/i]: each soldier to its own spot around the point, spread across your view.
    - [i]Hold & cover[/i]: the same, then crouched, each watching its own part of the way you looked.
    - [i]Stack up[/i]: on your side of the door, against the wall on both sides of the frame, facing it.
    - [i]Stack & clear[/i]: stacked, then the first two go into the room to its corners while the rest cover the doorway; "Room clear" when nobody shoots for a few seconds.
    - [i]Cover him[/i]: they keep close to that soldier wherever he goes.
    - [i]Lead the way[/i]: those soldiers become the pointmen (see below).
    - [i]Fall in[/i]: back to following you (cancels any order).
[*][b]Still fighting.[/b] Soldiers on a spot keep fighting the game's own way and come back to their spot afterwards: the game's AI follows our spot instead of you. Crouched watchers get up and fight when shots come near them, and go back to watching when it is over.
[*][b]Orders on your go.[/b] Press 0 while holding Z and the order waits; tap Z when you are ready and every waiting order starts at once (GO).
[*][b]No spot out of reach.[/b] A soldier that cannot get to its spot goes to the middle of the order instead of standing still.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics/main/docs/orders.jpg[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics/main/docs/hold-cover.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]Lead the way[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Pointmen.[/b] One or two soldiers of your ground squad (the nearest ones) go ahead of you along the way you are walking, about 6 and 9 m in front.
[*][b]To cover, not to the middle.[/b] Each pointman goes to its side of the corridor and stops against the wall when there is one, short of any wall ahead.
[*][b]Watching forward.[/b] At the spot they crouch and face the way you are going.
[*][b]Leapfrogging.[/b] When you catch up with a pointman, it moves on past the other one, which keeps watching. Run, and they run to the next spot.
[*][b]The rest of the squad[/b] follows you as usual.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics/main/docs/pointmen.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]Fights come first[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Gunfire hands them back.[/b] Your shots, an enemy's within 30 m of you or a pointman, or your squad's at a target that close: the pointmen go back to the game's own combat AI for a while, then take the lead again.
[*][b]Never left standing.[/b] A pointman with nowhere to go (a wall right ahead, no way through) follows you and fights as usual until it finds its next spot. Your squad crowding a narrow corridor does not stop them: soldiers in the way are not taken for walls.
[*][b]Only on foot.[/b] In a ship or on the hoverbike nothing changes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]On by default[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]"Lead the way" is on as soon as the mod is installed. "Fall in" for everyone from the order list switches it off; "Lead the way" from the list switches it on again.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]SpaceBourne 2 (Steam), with a ground squad (recruit soldiers for your faction).
[*][url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]UE4SS 3.0.1[/url] (the realism installer installs it for you).
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]

[b]A. SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer (recommended)[/b] Get it on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url] or [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism/releases/latest]GitHub[/url]. Tick Squad Tactics and any other mods of the set: it installs UE4SS if you don't have it, switches the mods on and keeps them updated.

[b]B. Manual[/b] (the zip on the [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics/releases]releases page[/url])
[list=1]
[*]Extract the zip into your game folder (...\SpaceBourne 2, the one with SpaceBourne2.exe). It creates SB2\Binaries\Win64\Mods\SquadTactics and switches itself on.
[*]No UE4SS yet? Get [url=https://github.com/UE4SS-RE/RE-UE4SS/releases/tag/v3.0.1]RE-UE4SS 3.0.1[/url] and copy dwmapi.dll, UE4SS.dll and UE4SS-settings.ini into SpaceBourne 2\SB2\Binaries\Win64\.
[/list]

[b]Uninstall:[/b] untick Squad Tactics in the installer or delete the SquadTactics folder. Squad Tactics never writes to your saves.

[line]
[size=5][b]Controls[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Z (tap)[/b]: The order that fits what you aim at
[*][b]Z (hold)[/b]: The order list: mouse up/down picks the order, left/right who; let go to give it
[*][b]0[/b]: Who gets the order: all, red, blue, the one or two nearest the spot
[*][b]0 while holding Z[/b]: The order waits for your go; then tap [b]Z[/b]: GO
[*][b]Shift+Z[/b]: Same as Z, so orders work while you sprint
[/list]

Orders work on foot only (in a ship Z is the game's free look). A gamepad layout is planned.

The key follows the realism set's shared key plan and can be changed in scripts\config.lua.

[line]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]

Edit Mods\SquadTactics\scripts\config.lua (every line is optional):

[list]
[*]Lead.Pointmen — 1 or 2 soldiers lead.
[*]Lead.Distance, Lead.SecondDistance, Lead.Leapfrog, Lead.MaxLead — how far ahead they go.
[*]Lead.LeapWhenAhead, Lead.YouMoved, Lead.MinHoldSeconds — when a pointman moves on.
[*]Lead.SideOffset, Lead.SideSearch, Lead.WallGap — how they pick their side of the corridor.
[*]Lead.Crouch — crouch at the spot.
[*]Lead.CombatRange, Lead.CombatSeconds — when gunfire hands them back to the game's combat AI.
[*]Lead.MaxRange, Lead.FloorHeight — a pointman this far away, or on another floor, goes back to the squad.
[*]Orders.Key, Orders.WhoKey, Orders.HoldTime, Orders.MenuStep — the order keys and the list.
[*]Orders.RedSize — how many soldiers are in the red team.
[*]Orders.Spread, Orders.HoldArc, Orders.DoorHalfWidth — how soldiers spread at a spot or a door.
[*]Orders.ClearAfter, Orders.ClearQuiet — when they go in, and when the room counts as clear.
[*]Lead.StartOn, Lead.Key (none by default), Messages.
[/list]

[line]
[size=5][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]No true cover map.[/b] The game gives mods no cover points, so a pointman picks "the side of the corridor, against the wall if there is one", found with a couple of line traces.
[*][b]Straight moves where there is no navigation data[/b] (station decks): a pointman then walks in a straight line to its spot and stops early if something is in the way.
[*][b]Silent Ops' quiet squad orders[/b] (F3) also steer the squad: use one or the other at a time.
[*][b]Doors[/b] are recognised by the game's door Blueprints (dungeon doors). Aimed at a plain doorway with no door, "Stack up" is still in the list (the wall around it is the frame).
[*][b]Finish the downed[/b] (Hardcore Tactical Realism's knocked-out enemies) and [b]patrols[/b] are planned, as is a gamepad layout.
[/list]

Design notes and plans (more orders, enemy patrols that leapfrog too): [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics/blob/main/DESIGN.md]DESIGN.md[/url]. Version history: [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]CHANGELOG.md[/url].

[line]
[size=5][b]The SpaceBourne 2 realism set[/b][/size]

Separate mods that work alone or in any combination. The [url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-Realism]SpaceBourne 2 Realism installer[/url] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/11]Nexus[/url]) installs the ones you tick and keeps them updated.

[list]
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HardcoreTacticalRealism]Hardcore Tactical Realism[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/4]Nexus[/url]): realistic ballistics, wounds and tactical AI. The core of the set.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SilentOps]Silent Ops[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/6]Nexus[/url]): stealth, silent takedowns and suppressors.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SquadTactics]Squad Tactics[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/18]Nexus[/url]): squad orders like Ready or Not, and your squad leads the way.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-AmmoDiscipline]Ammo Discipline[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/12]Nexus[/url]): carried ammo limits and scavenging, so every magazine counts.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GearWithoutLevels]Gear Without Levels[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/7]Nexus[/url]): use gear above your level, with small handling penalties.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalFirstPerson]Tactical First Person[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/15]Nexus[/url]): first person on foot, weapons held up, aiming down the sights.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-TacticalEngineering]Tactical Engineering[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/10]Nexus[/url]): realistic deployable turrets.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GetOutOfTheWay]Get Out of the Way[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/14]Nexus[/url]): NPCs step aside naturally when you walk through them.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-GroundWaypoints]Ground Waypoints[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/13]Nexus[/url]): planet waypoints on foot and on the hoverbike.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-FactionPower]Faction Power[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/9]Nexus[/url]): dungeons, strategic sales and missions earn your faction power.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-BiggerArmies]Bigger Armies[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/17]Nexus[/url]): twice the general slots for your faction's ground and space forces.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-ClearHUD]Clear HUD[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/16]Nexus[/url]): a reticle you can see and HUD colours of your choice.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-SplitControls]Split Controls[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/5]Nexus[/url]): separate vertical invert for ship and on foot, per device.
[*][b][url=https://github.com/hubertdungen/SpaceBourne2-HOTAS]SB2 HOTAS[/url][/b] ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/spacebourne2/mods/8]Nexus[/url]): HOTAS, rudder pedals, triple screens and head tracking.
[/list]

